  "answer_core": "You shouldn’t give Marcus 15% equity, a board seat, and a CTO title this week. Those are irreversible commitments, and you don’t yet know whether the partnership reduces or increases risk.\n\nUse Friday to set up a clear, time‑bound test. Tell him there is a real path to major upside, but only after evidence. Define a short sprint that shows whether he can deliver the platform work you need, whether it actually affects revenue, whether team continuity and knowledge transfer strengthen rather than concentrate the company around him, and whether his behavior fits the governance standard you need. Also spell out what success in that window would unlock.\n\nAvoid both premature commitment and vague delay. Give him a concrete, staged path tied to demonstrated impact, not hypothetical valuation math.",
